      "nets": ["GND", "5V_switched_CAN", "+5V"],
      "observed": "The isolated CAN transceivers U15 and U56 have their secondary-side ground pins (pin 5, GND2) tied to the same system GND net as their primary-side ground pins (pin 4, GND1). Their secondary supplies (pin 8, VCC2) are on 5V_switched_CAN, which is derived directly from system +5V through Q7 (Q7 source on +5V, Q7 drain on 5V_switched_CAN).",
      "expected": "For the intended isolated CAN buses, the transceiver secondary side (VCC2/GND2 and the CAN connector ground) should be on isolated rails/nets separate from the main GND/+5V system ground, so that galvanic isolation is preserved.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (`CAN0`, `CAN1`), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (`U8`, `U9`) through an isolated CAN transceiver (`U11`/companion)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"53\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"U15\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") ...) (node (ref \"U15\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") ...) (node (ref \"U56\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") ...) (node (ref \"U56\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"52\") (name \"5V_switched_CAN\") ... (node (ref \"U15\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"VCC2\") ...) (node (ref \"U56\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"VCC2\") ...) (node (ref \"Q7\") (pin \"3\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"+5V\") ... (node (ref \"Q7\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"S\") ...))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The CAN interfaces would not be galvanically isolated as intended; ground loops and common-mode faults would propagate between the rover ground and the external CAN devices, defeating the purpose of the isolated transceivers and potentially affecting reliability or safety.",
      "confidence": 0.72
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows isolated CAN transceivers U15 and U56 wired with their secondary ground tied to the system GND and their secondary supply derived from system +5V, which contradicts the specified isolated CAN bus architecture."
}

